<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Privacy manifest.

  The iOS equivalent of Android's data-safety form, and the cheapest credibility this app will ever
  get, so it is filled in precisely rather than defensively (spine: C3):

    NSPrivacyTracking            false  — there is no tracking code, and no network to do it over.
    NSPrivacyTrackingDomains     empty  — there are no domains. Not "none we contact": none exist.
    NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes  empty  — the app collects nothing. A report the user writes and
                                          sends from Mail is sent BY THEM, by an app that is not
                                          Arivu, after they have read it; it is not collection by
                                          this app, and the privacy policy says so in full (D-025 is
                                          the Android twin of this call).
    NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes    empty  — Arivu uses none of the required-reason APIs. It does not
                                          read file timestamps, disk space, system boot time, active
                                          keyboards or UserDefaults *of another app*. Its own
                                          UserDefaults use (the gate's cached pass, and "has a model
                                          ever loaded") is the app's own container, which category
                                          CA92.1 covers and which Apple does not require a reason
                                          entry for.

  VERIFY BEFORE SUBMISSION: if a future change reads free disk space through
  `NSFileSystemFreeSize`, or file timestamps, an NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes entry becomes mandatory.
  The gate reads free storage through `URLResourceValues.volumeAvailableCapacityForImportantUsage`,
  which is not on the required-reason list today. Re-check against Apple's current list at
  submission time; the list grows.

  UNVERIFIED: this file has never been validated by Xcode or by App Store Connect.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array/>
</dict>
</plist>
